# fresh_dev_blocks_no_destroy_task_reset_dies: A blocks-setup host whose RvgHostCallbacks leave destroy_task absent: bring-up and NOPs work (nothing destroys a task yet), then reset (DeviceCore::reset) writes root page 0, and DeviceCore::teardown_root, finding no destroy_task before it destroys the root task, ends the process (DeviceDeath::TeardownWithoutDestroyTask): the host dies at the reset. No user task is defined: the teardown would release it first, through DeviceCore::destroy_task, and the host would die there instead (DeviceDeath::NilBlock, as fresh_dev_blocks_no_destroy_task_delete_dies). Blocks setup only: the task and memory callbacks exist only there (a memory map with any of them is refused with RVG_ERR_MEMORY_CONFLICT, device_create_map_with_a_block).
